                <p rendition="#flush">I <hi rendition="#italic">Report by the Deputies</hi></p>
                <p>The Council heard and adopted the report of the 122nd meeting of the Deputies
                    submitted by M. Alphand, Acting Chairman.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">II <hi rendition="#italic">Peace Treaty With Italy: Free
                        Territory of Trieste</hi></p>
                <p>The Council considered the unagreed sections of the Deputies’ draft text of the
                    principles to be included in the Permanent Statute of the Free Territory (see
                    Annex to Record of 122nd Meeting of Deputies),<anchor n="65" xml:id="d365-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Withdrawal of
                    Troops</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to ask the Military Experts to submit
                    a recommendation on the figures to be inserted in the blank spaces in paragraph
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) of this text.</p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to delete the brackets around
                    paragraph (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>).</p>
                <pb facs="1362" n="1338" xml:id="pg1338"/>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Appointment of
                        Provisional Council of Government</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to defer a decision on the alternative
                    texts in square brackets until the Deputies had reported on the Permanent
                    Statute as a whole.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Elections to the
                        Constituent Assembly</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to adopt the whole of this text, the
                    brackets being deleted and the word “technically” substituted for the word
                    “materially” in the third paragraph.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>) It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to
                    adopt the text of the draft protocol concerning the appointment of a governor
                    for Trieste as recommended by the Deputies.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">III <hi rendition="#italic">Reports of the Committee of
                        Economic Experts</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">First Report</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Doc</hi>. <hi
                            rendition="#italic">CFM</hi>(<hi rendition="#italic">46</hi>) (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">NY</hi>)<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >17</hi>)<anchor n="66" xml:id="d365-f2"/></p>
                <p>The Council <hi rendition="#italic">adopted</hi> this report and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">approved</hi> the texts contained in it.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Second Report</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Doc</hi>. <hi
                            rendition="#italic">CFM</hi>(<hi rendition="#italic">46</hi>) (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">NY</hi>)<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >20</hi>)<anchor n="67" xml:id="d365-f3"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>1. <hi rendition="#italic">Contracts</hi>, (<hi rendition="#italic">page
                            3</hi>). The additional paragraph 2(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)
                        proposed by the United Kingdom representative was <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >agreed</hi>, as well as the text submitted by the Economic
                        Committee.</item>
                    <label/>
                    <item>In this connection, the special provision relating to the U.S. was <hi
                            rendition="#italic">agreed.</hi></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Periods of Prescription</hi>. The text submitted
                        for Part II of Annex VII of the Italian Treaty, and for Part II of Annex V
                        of the other treaties was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed.</hi></item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Miscellaneous Provisions</hi>. The U.K. delegate
                        withdrew Part IV of Annex VII of the Italian Treaty and Part IV of Annex V
                        of the other treaties.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Claims on Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >page 5</hi>). The text proposed by the United States Delegation was
                        approved for inclusion in the Peace Treaties with Italy, Roumania, Bulgaria
                        and Hungary. The first three paragraphs of the United States text were
                        approved for inclusion in the Peace Treaty with Finland.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Insurance</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">pages 6
                            and 7</hi>). The text proposed by the United Kingdom Delegation as set
                        out in paragraph 2 was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> and that set out
                        in paragraph 5 was adopted with the period of 3 years amended to 18
                        months.</item>
                    <label>6.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">Petroleum</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">page
                            8</hi>). The text proposed by the United Kingdom representative to be
                        added to the end of Article 24, paragraph 1, of the Roumanian Treaty was <hi
                            rendition="#italic">agreed</hi>, subject to an amendment by the U.S.S.R.
                        Delegation. The amended text read as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                            <p>“If necessary the Roumanian Government shall revoke legislation
                                enacted since September 1, 1939, <hi rendition="#italic">in so far
                                    as it discriminates against</hi> the rights of United Nations
                                nationals.”</p>
                        </quote></item>
                </list>
                <pb facs="1363" n="1339" xml:id="pg1339"/>
                <p>In this connection the U.S.S.R. representative proposed the deletion from the
                    Roumanian Treaty of Article 30 bis dealing with the question of fair market
                    prices. After an exchange of views it was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to
                    defer further consideration of the question until later.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Third Report</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Docs</hi>. <hi
                            rendition="#italic">CFM</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">46</hi>)(<hi
                            rendition="#italic">NY</hi>)<hi rendition="#italic">29 and
                        30</hi>)<anchor n="68" xml:id="d365-f4"/></p>
                <p>The Council proceeded to consider the unagreed sections of these reports on Annex
                    III of the Peace Treaty with Italy and the related provisions of Article 69 with
                    the following results: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Transfer of State and Para-statal
                                Property</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">page 2</hi>). The new
                            paragraph 1A recommended by the Committee was <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >agreed</hi> with the deletion of the brackets round the concluding
                            phrase.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Works of Art, etc., Removed from Ceded
                                Territory</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">page 3</hi>). The new
                            paragraph 1C was <hi rendition="#italic">adopted</hi>, the French
                            Delegation having withdrawn their objections to its inclusion.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Public Debt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">page
                                4</hi>). The text proposed for paragraph 3 was <hi
                                rendition="#italic">adopted</hi> with the deletion of all the
                            brackets.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Italian Pension Obligations</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">page 5</hi>). The new paragraph 4A recommended
                            by the Committee was <hi rendition="#italic">adopted</hi> with the
                            deletion of the brackets round the words “or military”.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Concessionary companies</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">page 5</hi>). This question was <hi
                                rendition="#italic">reserved</hi> pending final agreement on the
                            problem of reparation.</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Property removed from Ceded Territory</hi>
                                (<hi rendition="#italic">page 7</hi>). The text proposed for the new
                            paragraph 10A on this subject was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi>,
                            subject to the words “during the war” being amended to read “after
                            September 3, 1943”.</item>
                        <label>7.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Subparagraph</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >g</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">of paragraph 5, Article 69</hi>
                                (<hi rendition="#italic">page 9</hi>). The text proposed for this
                            subparagraph by the French and U.S.S.R. representatives was <hi
                                rendition="#italic">agreed</hi>.<anchor n="68a" xml:id="d365-f5"
                            /></item>
                        <label>8.</label>
                        <item>The remainder of the text in CFM (46)
                                (NY) 30 was <hi rendition="#italic">approved.</hi></item>
                    </list></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">IV <hi rendition="#italic">Regime of the Danube</hi></p>
                <p>The U.S.S.R. representative submitted the text of a proposal dealing with this
                    question to be recorded as a decision of the Council of Foreign Ministers. The
                    provisional English text read as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Navigation in the Danube shall be free and open on terms of equality in
                            so far as this concerns port and navigation charges and conditions of
                            commercial shipping within the limits of the usual commercial relations,
                            to the nationals, vessels of commerce and goods of all states.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <pb facs="1364" n="1340" xml:id="pg1340"/>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to refer this text to the Deputies for
                    drafting and with a view to its eventual inclusion as a Peace Treaty
                    article.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">V <hi rendition="#italic">Next Meetings of the
                    Council</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <item>Deputies—November 29, 1946, at 11 a.m.</item>
                    <item>Ministers—November 29, 1946, at 4 p.m.</item>
                    <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi>, November 29, 1946.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
